---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Transport Guide — Getting Around China';
const description = 'How to use trains, subways, Didi, and buses in Chinese cities.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="py-12 text-center">
      <div class="text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium mb-2">CATEGORY</div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900  ">Transport Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-500  ">Getting around Chinese cities — trains, subways, taxis, and more.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose prose-gray  ">
      <div class="bg-amber-50  :border-amber-900 rounded-xl p-4 mb-8">
        <p class="text-amber-800  ">
          <strong>Note:</strong> Detailed transport guides coming soon.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h2>High-Speed Rail (高铁)</h2>
      <p>China's high-speed rail network is the largest in the world. With speeds up to 350 km/h, it's often faster than flying for trips under 1,000 km.</p>
      <h2>Subway Systems</h2>
      <p>Major cities like Beijing, Shanghai, and Shenzhen have extensive subway networks. Most accept Alipay or WeChat Pay directly at the gate.</p>
      <h2>Didi (China's Uber)</h2>
      <p>Didi is the dominant ride-hailing app. Foreign credit cards are now accepted, and the app has an English interface option.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
